<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113073" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκ-εών</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶνος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>forge, smithy,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βῆ ῥ᾽ ἴμεν ἐς χαλκεῶνα</span> [where
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εω</span> must be pronounced as one syll.]
				<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.273
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.41
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bar of wrought iron,</i> Lat. <i>strictura,</i> glossed
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυσητήρ, χαλκεών</span> (nisi leg.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκέων</span>),
		<u>Gloss.</u>
        </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
